{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfryYEa1iCW6n9yRqMazg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `logstats/parse.py` and added `tests/test_parse.py`. All 26 tests pass with `python -m pytest`.\n\nPlain `pytest` fails at collection with an import error, because `logstats` isn't on the import path when run that way. I did not change that. A root `conftest.py` or a `pythonpath` setting would fix it if you want plain `pytest` to work.\n\n**What's in `parse.py`**\n- `parse_line` splits on whitespace and needs 5 or 6 fields. It returns `None` for malformed lines.\n- The timestamp must be timezone-aware. It is converted to UTC.\n- `status` must be three digits in the 1xx to 5xx range. `latency_ms` and `bytes` must be plain non-negative decimal numbers. This rejects `nan`, `inf`, `1e3`, and negatives.\n- `summarize` counts malformed lines and aggregates the rest. Percentiles are nearest-rank. `top_paths` sorts by count descending, then path ascending, and keeps five.\n- Running `summarize` on `sample.log` gives 5 parsed records and 1 malformed line.\n\n**Judgment calls the spec didn't settle**\n- A timestamp with no timezone is malformed. FORMAT.md says the timestamps are UTC, so I read a missing offset as a format error.\n- Blank lines are counted as malformed, since the spec says any non-matching line is malformed.\n- Status must be between 100 and 599. A `99` status is malformed.\n- `datetime.fromisoformat` accepts `Z` only on Python 3.11 and later. The environment has 3.14.\n\nThe `tests/` directory is untracked, so the new file shows up in `git status` as `?? tests/test_parse.py`. I removed the `__pycache__` and `.pytest_cache` directories my test runs created."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4812,"cache_read_input_tokens":45882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_